# Recorded outcome of `make -C tb frozen && make -C tb check-frozen`, i.e. the 2001
# port of binutils 2.11.2 (tb/ref.7z) built on a current host, linking the 2001
# precompiled objects (tb/base2001.7z), against the reference ROMs base.7z ships.
#
# The 2001 toolchain does not reproduce those ROMs and is not expected to: it does
# not carry the stock 2.47 `lang_one_common` alignment, so every internal-RAM
# address after .bss sits 8 bytes lower. What must not change unnoticed is HOW FAR
# it is. `tb/romdiff.py --expect` reads this file and exits nonzero on any movement,
# which is what makes .github/workflows/frozen.yml able to go red.
#
# Reproduced here on ubuntu-24.04 / gcc 13.3.0-m32, byte-for-byte the counts in
# tb/frozen-report.md, "Convergence" (GitHub run 32878917600).
#
# diag does not link under 2.11.2: `lib/www51.sc:266: undefined symbol `_reti_'
# referenced in expression`. 2.11.2 folds a PROVIDE's right-hand side before it
# consults the destination, so the ten unused interrupt trampolines have to resolve
# even though diag references none of them. A linker difference, not an object one.
#
# project  outcome       differing bytes
diag       not-produced
ds1620     differ        217
ds1822     differ        225
lcd        differ        214
led1       differ        213
led2       differ        214
led3       differ        214
serial     differ        325
welcome    differ        213
wjava      differ        213
